{
  "mn152:0.1": "Middle Discourses 152 ",
  "mn152:0.2": "The Development of the Faculties ",
  "mn152:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn152:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Kajaṅgalā in a bamboo grove. ",
  "mn152:2.1": "Then the student Uttara, a pupil of the brahmin Pārāsariya, approached the Buddha, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "mn152:2.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side. The Buddha said to him, ",
  "mn152:2.3": "“Uttara, does Pārāsariya teach his disciples the development of the faculties?” ",
  "mn152:2.4": "“He does, worthy Gotama.” ",
  "mn152:2.5": "“But how does he teach it?” ",
  "mn152:2.6": "“Worthy Gotama, it’s when the eye sees no sight and the ear hears no sound. ",
  "mn152:2.7": "That’s how Pārāsariya teaches his disciples the development of the faculties.” ",
  "mn152:2.8": "“In that case, Uttara, a blind person and a deaf person will have developed faculties ",
  "mn152:2.9": "according to what Pārāsariya says. ",
  "mn152:2.10": "For a blind person sees no sight with their eyes and a deaf person hears no sound with their ears.” ",
  "mn152:2.11": "When he said this, Uttara sat silent, dismayed, shoulders drooping, downcast, depressed, with nothing to say. ",
  "mn152:3.1": "Knowing this, the Buddha addressed Venerable Ānanda, ",
  "mn152:3.2": "“Ānanda, the development of the faculties taught by Pārāsariya is quite different from the supreme development of the faculties in the tr